1. `rev11_regression_test.go` checks `checkpointSeal` and `checkpointSealToken` construction only as `ast.CompositeLit` (around lines 837–845). `TestReview14AdditionalGateShapes/mint_seal_without_composite` adds a compiling production function using `v := new(checkpointSeal); v.token = new(checkpointSealToken); v.sessionID = "invented"; return v`. The real census returns nil. This violates the new source/documentation claim that only the free `admitCheckpoint` constructs the seal/token. No raw/admittedCheckpoint spelling is needed in this producer. `TestReview14FieldAssembledRuntime` independently shows a non-nil self-minted token passes `authority` and derives a creation profile. That latter test is helper-level evidence only: a complete outer capability assembled in an ordinary new production function IS rejected by the current census. Do not misreport the combination as an external Reader exploit.
